::: lead
Learn how to create a visual weather widget that automatically conforms to your active dashboard theme by combining a Text widget, Markdown, and AI-generated HomeyScript [badge: Homey Pro].
:::
![content: Weather forcast](help/images/tip_weather_forecast_01.jpg)
To maintain a consistent visual style across your dashboard, you can build a clean, native weather forecast. Rather than copying and pasting web snippets from external pages, which introduces mismatched styles and layout issues, you should fetch data from public APIs and parse it into native widgets. This guide uses HomeyScript to retrieve weather data and formats it into Markdown. The **Text** widget then displays the result, ensuring perfect integration with any active theme.

### 1. Generating the Scripts with AI

Generative AI chat models (such as Gemini, ChatGPT, or Claude) are excellent at writing HomeyScript code. You can prompt them to create custom Markdown outputs.

To help the AI generate the correct syntax, copy the markdown rules from the [Markdown Formatting Reference](help://Data%20Types%20%26%20Formats/markdown-formatting) section in this help guide and paste them into your prompt.

#### Prompt Example for Amsterdam:
> I am using the Homey app "Dashboard Studio" and want to create a 7 day weather widget for "Amsterdam". Could you help me with the Homeyscript code to generate a horizontal markdown table for the text widget? Inside each cell, I need the day in English, a weather icon like a cloud or sun, the max temperature as just a number with no label, and the min temperature as just a number with no label. This is the help file with the specialised markdown that can be used: [pasted Markdown reference rules]

---

### 2. The Weather Scripts

Below are two finalized scripts. They use the free Open-Meteo API to retrieve geocoding and forecast data.

#### Script 1: 7-Day Forecast
This script finds coordinates for your location, retrieves the daily temperature ranges, and outputs a horizontal Markdown table.

::: code-block 7-Day Forecast Script
// --- Configuration ---
const LOCATION = "Amsterdam";
const ICON_SIZE = 50; // Size in pixels
const TIMEZONE = "Europe/Amsterdam";

try {
  // 1. Geocoding step to find coordinates
  const geoUrl = `https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search?name=${encodeURIComponent(LOCATION)}&count=1&format=json`;
  const geoResponse = await fetch(geoUrl);
  if (!geoResponse.ok) throw new Error(`Geocoding fetch failed: ${geoResponse.status}`);

  const geoData = await geoResponse.json();
  if (!geoData.results || geoData.results.length === 0) throw new Error(`Location not found: ${LOCATION}`);

  const lat = geoData.results[0].latitude;
  const lon = geoData.results[0].longitude;

  // 2. Weather forecast step using coordinates
  const url = `https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=${lat}&longitude=${lon}&daily=weather_code,temperature_2m_max,temperature_2m_min&timezone=${encodeURIComponent(TIMEZONE)}`;
  const response = await fetch(url);
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Weather fetch failed: ${response.status}`);

  const data = await response.json();
  const daily = data.daily;

  const daysEnglish = ["Sunday", "Monday", "Tuesday", "Wednesday", "Thursday", "Friday", "Saturday"];

  function getWeatherIcon(code) {
    let iconName = "ph-cloud";
    if (code === 0) iconName = "sun"; 
    if ([1, 2, 3].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-sun"; 
    if ([45, 48].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-fog"; 
    if ([51, 53, 55, 56, 57].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-snow"; 
    if ([61, 63, 65, 66, 67, 80, 81, 82].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-rain"; 
    if ([71, 73, 75, 77, 85, 86].includes(code)) iconName = "snowflake"; 
    if ([95, 96, 99].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-lightning";

    return `:ph-${iconName}|${ICON_SIZE}:`;
  }

  let rowDays  = "|";
  let rowSeps  = "|";
  let rowIcons = "|";
  let rowMax   = "|";
  let rowMin   = "|";

  for (let i = 0; i < 7; i++) {
    const date = new Date(daily.time[i]);
    const dayName = daysEnglish[date.getDay()];
    const icon = getWeatherIcon(daily.weather_code[i]);
    const maxTemp = Math.round(daily.temperature_2m_max[i]) + "°C";
    const minTemp = Math.round(daily.temperature_2m_min[i]) + "°C";

    rowDays  += ` ${dayName} |`;
    rowSeps  += ` :---: |`; 
    rowIcons += ` ${icon} |`; 
    rowMax   += ` ${maxTemp} |`;
    rowMin   += ` ${minTemp} |`;
  }

  return `${rowDays}\n${rowSeps}\n${rowIcons}\n${rowMax}\n${rowMin}\n`;

} catch (error) {
  return `Error: ${error.message}`;
}
:::

#### Script 2: 6-Hour Forecast
This script retrieves the current temperature, wind speed, humidity, and barometric pressure. It also generates a horizontal table showing the forecasted conditions for the next 6 hours.

::: code-block 6-Hour Forecast Script
// --- Configuration ---
const LOCATION = "Amsterdam";
const ICON_SIZE = 50; // Size in pixels
const TIMEZONE = "Europe/Amsterdam";

try {
  // 1. Geocoding step to find coordinates
  const geoUrl = `https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search?name=${encodeURIComponent(LOCATION)}&count=1&format=json`;
  const geoResponse = await fetch(geoUrl);
  if (!geoResponse.ok) throw new Error(`Geocoding fetch failed: ${geoResponse.status}`);

  const geoData = await geoResponse.json();
  if (!geoData.results || geoData.results.length === 0) throw new Error(`Location not found: ${LOCATION}`);

  const lat = geoData.results[0].latitude;
  const lon = geoData.results[0].longitude;

  // 2. Weather forecast step using coordinates
  const url = `https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=${lat}&longitude=${lon}&current=temperature_2m,relative_humidity_2m,wind_speed_10m,surface_pressure&hourly=temperature_2m,weather_code&timezone=${encodeURIComponent(TIMEZONE)}`;
  const response = await fetch(url);
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Weather fetch failed: ${response.status}`);

  const data = await response.json();
  const current = data.current;
  const hourly = data.hourly;

  function getWeatherIcon(code) {
    let iconName = "ph-cloud"; 
    if (code === 0) iconName = "sun"; 
    if ([1, 2, 3].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-sun"; 
    if ([45, 48].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-fog"; 
    if ([51, 53, 55, 56, 57].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-snow"; 
    if ([61, 63, 65, 66, 67, 80, 81, 82].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-rain"; 
    if ([71, 73, 75, 77, 85, 86].includes(code)) iconName = "snowflake"; 
    if ([95, 96, 99].includes(code)) iconName = "cloud-lightning"; 

    return `:ph-${iconName}|${ICON_SIZE}:`;
  }

  const now = new Date();
  let startIndex = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < hourly.time.length; i++) {
    const d = new Date(hourly.time[i]);
    if (d.getTime() > now.getTime() - 60 * 60 * 1000) {
      startIndex = i;
      break;
    }
  }

  const currentTemp = Math.round(current.temperature_2m) + "°C";
  const windSpeed = current.wind_speed_10m.toFixed(1);
  const humidity = current.relative_humidity_2m;
  const pressureMmHg = Math.round(current.surface_pressure * 0.750062);

  let markdown = `:ph-thermometer: ${currentTemp} &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; :ph-wind: ${windSpeed} m/s &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; :ph-drop: ${humidity}% &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; :ph-gauge: ${pressureMmHg} mmHg\n---\n`;

  let rowHours = "|";
  let rowSeps  = "|";
  let rowIcons = "|";
  let rowTemps = "|";

  for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
    const idx = startIndex + i;
    if (idx >= hourly.time.length) break;

    const d = new Date(hourly.time[idx]);
    const hours = String(d.getHours()).padStart(2, '0');
    const minutes = String(d.getMinutes()).padStart(2, '0');
    const timeStr = `${hours}:${minutes}`;

    const icon = getWeatherIcon(hourly.weather_code[idx]);
    const temp = Math.round(hourly.temperature_2m[idx]) + "°C";

    rowHours += ` ${timeStr} |`;
    rowSeps  += ` :---: |`;
    rowIcons += ` ${icon} |`; 
    rowTemps += ` ${temp} |`;
  }

  return `${markdown}${rowHours}\n${rowSeps}\n${rowIcons}\n${rowTemps}\n`;

} catch (error) {
  return `Error: ${error.message}`;
}
:::

---

### 3. Setting Up the Homey Flow [badge: Homey Pro]

To execute the scripts periodically and push the resulting Markdown to the dashboard, create a new flow in Homey.

1. **Trigger:** Choose a trigger card such as **Every 1 hour** or **The time is...**.
2. **Execute Scripts:** Add two HomeyScript action cards to execute the scripts created in the previous step.
3. **Send to Dashboard:** Under the **Then** section, add two Dashboard Studio action cards: **Send [HomeyScript: result] to Dashboard**. Assign unique event names for each card, such as `weather7day` and `weather5hr`.
4. **First Run:** Right-click the trigger card in the flow editor and select **Start test** or **Execute from here** to run the flow immediately. This will initialize the data topics.

![content: Flow](help/images/tip_weather_forecast_02.jpg)
---

### 4. Configuring the Text Widget

Once the flow has run, you can configure your dashboard to display the forecasts.

1. Open the Dashboard Studio editor.
2. Add a **Text** widget to your canvas.
3. In the widget's settings, locate the **Text Content** property under the **Label & Text** section.
4. Enter the topic placeholders inside your text. The widget will automatically replace them with the Markdown payload sent from your flow:

::: code-block Dynamic Text Content
# :ph-thermometer-simple: 7-Day Weather Forecast for Amsterdam
---
{{weather7day}}

{{weather5hr}}
:::

![content: Settings](help/images/tip_weather_forecast_03.jpg)

#### Recommended Styling Adjustments
To ensure the widget blends perfectly with your canvas, apply the following settings in the widget editor:

In the **Markdown** section:

* Set the **Table Style** to **Solid Header**
* Set the **Table Column Width Mode** to **Equal Table Column Widths**
* Set the **Markdown Icon Style** to **Duotone**

![content: Styles](help/images/tip_weather_forecast_04.jpg)

The weather forecast will now dynamically render on your dashboard. When you switch dashboard themes, the widget colors and typography will automatically update to match the new theme.

::: lead
Want headlines from your favourite sites on a wall dashboard or a browser start page? Dashboard Studio includes a dedicated [Fetch RSS Feed to Markdown](help://Homey%20Flow%20Cards/rss-feeds) flow card that turns RSS or Atom news feeds into a live [Markdown](help://Data%20Types%20%26%20Formats/markdown-formatting) table for your [Text](help://Widgets/text) widget with zero coding required. [badge: Homey Pro]
:::

![content: RSS news reader on a dashboard](help/images/tip_rss_news_01.jpg)

::: alert info rss
**Native Flow Card Available**

Dashboard Studio now provides a dedicated native [Fetch RSS Feed to Markdown](help://Homey%20Flow%20Cards/rss-feeds) flow card. It handles feed downloading, polite in-memory caching, multi-feed aggregation, custom icons and badges, and Markdown generation in a single card with zero programming required.

The HomeyScript method below is redundant for everyday dashboard use. It is preserved here for developers and tinkerers who want to build their own custom RSS scripts, experiment with custom XML parsing, or tailor specialized data formats in JavaScript.
:::

RSS is a small XML file that a website publishes so other apps can read new articles without opening the site. Newsrooms, blogs, and many public organisations still offer one. Dashboard Studio downloads it, and paints it as a clean table.

::: alert info rss
**Where to find a feed**

Look for an orange RSS icon, a **Subscribe** link, or a URL that ends in `rss.xml`, `/feed`, or `/atom.xml`. BBC publishes a directory of feeds at [BBC News RSS](https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/10628323 ^). Other public examples:

* [BBC News](https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/rss.xml ^)
* [BBC Technology](https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml ^)
* [NOS Algemeen](https://feeds.nos.nl/nosnieuwsalgemeen ^)
* [NASA Breaking News](https://www.nasa.gov/rss/dyn/breaking_news.rss ^)
* [NPR News](https://feeds.npr.org/1001/rss.xml ^)
:::

### Quickest setup: The Fetch RSS flow card (Recommended)

The fastest and most memory-friendly way to display news is using Dashboard Studio's native **Fetch RSS Feed to Markdown** action card.

1. Create a flow triggered by **Dashboard Loaded / Refreshed** (or a recurring timer like **Every 15 minutes**).
2. Add the action card **Fetch RSS Feed to Markdown**.
3. In **RSS / Atom URL(s)**, paste your feed address. For multiple feeds, put each URL on its own line.
4. Set **Dashboard Topic** to `rssfeed`. The card downloads, parses, and sends the table to `homey/event/rssfeed` in a single step.
5. In your dashboard, bind a **Text** widget to topic `rssfeed`.

The card automatically caches articles for 5 minutes and streams incoming feeds with early abort, keeping your Homey fast and polite to news servers. Read the full [RSS Feeds Guide](help://Homey%20Flow%20Cards/rss-feeds) for multi-feed badge styling and layout options.

---

### Alternative: Custom HomeyScript

If you prefer to write custom parsing code or manipulate tags in JavaScript, you can still use the original HomeyScript pattern:

1. A Homey Flow runs when your dashboard opens.
2. HomeyScript downloads the feed and returns Markdown.
3. **Send … with value … to Dashboard** pushes that Markdown onto a topic.
4. A **Text** widget binds **Text Content** to that topic.

You need the **HomeyScript** app on Homey Pro, plus Dashboard Studio.

### 1. The Homey Flow

Create a new Advanced Flow (or a standard flow). The chain is:

**When** [Dashboard Loaded / Refreshed](help://Homey%20Flow%20Cards/loading-saving#dashboard-loaded-refreshed) → **And** Dashboard Name contains your file name → **Then** HomeyScript → **Then** [Send … with value … to Dashboard](help://Homey%20Flow%20Cards/send-receive-data#then-send-with-value-to-dashboard).

![content: RSS Homey Flow](help/images/tip_rss_news_02.png)

#### When: Dashboard Loaded / Refreshed

This trigger fires when a browser opens or refreshes a dashboard. Use it so the headlines are fresh the moment someone looks at the page.

#### And: Dashboard Name contains …

The When card exposes a **Dashboard Name** tag (the saved file name without `.json`). Add a Logic **And** card that checks **Text contains**, drop **Dashboard Name** into it, and type the dashboard that should show the news (for example `startpage` or `homepage`).

If you only have one dashboard file, you can leave this And card out.

#### Then: HomeyScript

1. Open the **HomeyScript** app and create a new script. Name it something clear, such as `RSS to Markdown`.
2. Paste the script from the next section and save.
3. In the flow, add a HomeyScript **Then** card and pick that script.

The card’s **Result** tag is the Markdown string the script `return`s.

#### Then: Send … with value … to Dashboard

* **Event Name:** invent a short topic, for example `rssfeed`. This becomes `homey/event/rssfeed` on the dashboard.
* **Value:** insert the HomeyScript **Result** tag.

::: alert info timer
**How often to refresh**

**Dashboard Loaded / Refreshed** already updates when someone opens the page. For a tablet that stays on all day, add a second flow with **Every 15 minutes** (or slower) that runs the same script and Send card. News hosts often limit faster polling.
:::

### 2. Add a Text widget

1. In **Create Widget**, pick **Text** and click **Add**. See [Widgets](help://Widgets) if you are new to placing widgets.
2. Select the widget. In **Text Settings**, find **Text Content**.
3. Click the **Link Icon** :ph-bold ph-link text-slate-400: next to **Text Content** so the whole field is dynamic. See [Connecting Widgets & Data (Topics)](help://Connecting%20Widgets%20%26%20Data%20%28Topics%29#custom-topic-names).
4. Set the topic to `rssfeed` (or paste `homey/event/rssfeed` from **Data Stream Explorer**). Both forms work.

Run the flow once from Homey (**Test** / **Start**) so the topic has a value. The table should appear in the widget.

::: alert info paint-brush
**Make the table match your theme**

Open **Markdown** on the Text widget:

* **Table Style** to a dense preset (for example **Solid Header** or **Classic**)
* **Table Column Width Mode** to **Equal Table Column Widths** if the columns feel uneven

Headlines use Dashboard Studio Markdown, including `[cell @markerTint1]` chips, `:ph-newspaper:` icons, and `[color @textMuted]` excerpts. Theme tokens such as `@markerTint1` follow the dashboard theme. You can also set a fixed color with a hex value such as `#E11D48`. Full syntax lives in the [Markdown Formatting Reference](help://Data%20Types%20%26%20Formats/markdown-formatting). Article links in the script use a trailing `^` so they open in a new browser tab.
:::

::: alert info text-aa
**Tighten the title and excerpt**

Each headline is **Header 3** (`###`). If the gap under the title looks too large, select the **Text** widget, open **Text & Typography**, then **Header 3**, and lower **Vertical Spacing (px)**. A value around `-15` pulls the excerpt up.

![content: Header 3 vertical spacing](help/images/tip_rss_news_03.png)
:::

### 3. Start with one feed

Paste this script into HomeyScript. Only the `CONFIG` object at the top is meant to be edited.

::: code-block Single RSS feed
// HomeyScript: RSS feed to Dashboard Studio Markdown
// Paste this into a HomeyScript, then send the Result tag to Dashboard Studio.

const CONFIG = {
  maxItems: 15,

  showTimestamp: true,
  showTime: true,
  showDay: true,
  showTimeAboveDate: true,

  showExcerpt: true,
  maxExcerptLength: 240,

  showImage: true,
  imageSize: '200',

  // Column keys: 'source', 'image', 'headline', 'timestamp'
  // The source column hides automatically when you have only one feed.
  columnOrder: ['source', 'image', 'headline', 'timestamp'],

  feeds: [
    {
      url: 'https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/rss.xml',
      label: 'BBC News',
      icon: 'newspaper',
      color: '@markerTint1', // theme token, or a hex such as '#E11D48'
      maxExcerpts: 15
    }
  ]
};

const COLUMN_META = {
  source: { title: 'Source', align: ':---' },
  image: { title: 'Image', align: ':---:' },
  headline: { title: 'Headline', align: ':---' },
  timestamp: { title: 'Published', align: ':---:' }
};

async function run() {
  let allItems = [];
  const excerptCounters = {};

  for (const feed of CONFIG.feeds) {
    excerptCounters[feed.url] = 0;
    const items = await fetchAndParseFeed(feed);
    allItems = allItems.concat(items);
  }

  allItems.sort((a, b) => b.date - a.date);
  allItems = allItems.slice(0, CONFIG.maxItems);

  const activeColumns = CONFIG.columnOrder.filter(col => {
    if (col === 'timestamp' && !CONFIG.showTimestamp) return false;
    if (col === 'source' && CONFIG.feeds.length <= 1) return false;
    if (col === 'image' && !CONFIG.showImage) return false;
    return true;
  });

  let markdown = '';
  markdown += '| ' + activeColumns.map(col => COLUMN_META[col].title).join(' | ') + ' |\n';
  markdown += '| ' + activeColumns.map(col => COLUMN_META[col].align).join(' | ') + ' |\n';

  for (const item of allItems) {
    const rowCells = activeColumns.map(col => {
      switch (col) {
        case 'source': {
          const bgPrefix = item.feed.color ? `[cell ${item.feed.color}] ` : '';
          const cleanIcon = item.feed.icon ? item.feed.icon.replace(/^ph-/, '') : '';
          const iconString = cleanIcon ? `:ph-${cleanIcon}|20: ` : '';
          const labelString = item.feed.label || '';
          return `${bgPrefix}${iconString}${labelString}`.trim();
        }
        case 'image':
          if (item.image) {
            const sizeModifier = CONFIG.imageSize ? `|${CONFIG.imageSize}` : '';
            return `![${sizeModifier}](${item.image})`;
          }
          return '';
        case 'headline': {
          let cellContent = `### [${item.title}](${item.link} ^)`;
          const maxAllowedExcerpts = item.feed.maxExcerpts !== undefined ? item.feed.maxExcerpts : CONFIG.maxItems;
          if (CONFIG.showExcerpt && item.excerpt) {
            if (excerptCounters[item.feed.url] < maxAllowedExcerpts) {
              cellContent += `<br>[color @textMuted]${item.excerpt}[/color]`;
              excerptCounters[item.feed.url]++;
            }
          }
          return cellContent;
        }
        case 'timestamp':
          return formatRelativeDate(item.date, CONFIG.showTime, CONFIG.showDay, CONFIG.showTimeAboveDate);
        default:
          return '';
      }
    });
    markdown += '| ' + rowCells.join(' | ') + ' |\n';
  }

  if (typeof global.setTagValue === 'function') {
    await global.setTagValue('dashboard_rss_feed', { type: 'string', title: 'Dashboard RSS Feed' }, markdown);
  }

  console.log(markdown);
  return markdown;
}

async function fetchAndParseFeed(feed) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(feed.url);
    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP Status ${response.status}`);
    const xml = await response.text();

    const isAtom = xml.includes('<entry>');
    const nodeRegex = isAtom ? /<entry>([\s\S]*?)<\/entry>/g : /<item>([\s\S]*?)<\/item>/g;
    const nodes = xml.match(nodeRegex);
    if (!nodes) return [];

    return nodes.map(node => {
      const title = extractTagValue(node, 'title');
      const link = isAtom ? extractAtomLink(node) : extractTagValue(node, 'link');
      const dateStr = isAtom
        ? (extractTagValue(node, 'updated') || extractTagValue(node, 'published'))
        : (extractTagValue(node, 'pubDate') || extractTagValue(node, 'dc:date'));
      const rawExcerpt = extractTagValue(node, isAtom ? 'summary' : 'description');

      return {
        title: sanitizePlainText(title, 0),
        link: String(link || '').trim(),
        excerpt: sanitizeExcerpt(rawExcerpt, CONFIG.maxExcerptLength),
        image: extractImageUrl(node),
        date: dateStr ? new Date(dateStr) : new Date(0),
        feed: feed
      };
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`[Feed Error] Failed fetching ${feed.url}:`, error.message);
    return [];
  }
}

function extractTagValue(xmlBlock, tagName) {
  const match = xmlBlock.match(new RegExp(`<${tagName}(?:\\s+[^>]*)?>([\\s\\S]*?)<\/${tagName}>`, 'i'));
  if (!match) return '';
  return match[1].replace(/<!\[CDATA\[([\s\S]*?)\]\]>/gi, '$1').trim();
}

function extractAtomLink(xmlBlock) {
  const hrefMatch = xmlBlock.match(/<link\s+[^>]*href=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  return hrefMatch ? hrefMatch[1] : extractTagValue(xmlBlock, 'link');
}

function extractImageUrl(xmlBlock) {
  let match = xmlBlock.match(/<enclosure\s+[^>]*url=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  if (match) return match[1];
  match = xmlBlock.match(/<media:(?:content|thumbnail)\s+[^>]*url=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  if (match) return match[1];
  match = xmlBlock.match(/<img\s+[^>]*src=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  if (match) return match[1];
  return null;
}

function decodeHtmlEntities(text) {
  return String(text || '')
    .replace(/&nbsp;/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/&#(\d+);/g, function (_, n) { return String.fromCharCode(parseInt(n, 10)); })
    .replace(/&#x([0-9a-f]+);/gi, function (_, n) { return String.fromCharCode(parseInt(n, 16)); })
    .replace(/&quot;/g, '"')
    .replace(/&apos;|&#39;/g, "'")
    .replace(/&lt;/g, '<')
    .replace(/&gt;/g, '>')
    .replace(/&amp;/g, '&');
}

function stripHtmlTags(text) {
  return String(text || '')
    .replace(/<script[\s\S]*?<\/script>/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/<style[\s\S]*?<\/style>/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ');
}

function stripUrls(text) {
  return String(text || '')
    .replace(/https?:\/\/[^\s<>"']+/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/www\.[^\s<>"']+/gi, ' ');
}

function collapseSpaces(text) {
  return String(text || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
}

function toPlainText(rawText) {
  let text = decodeHtmlEntities(rawText);
  text = decodeHtmlEntities(text);
  text = stripHtmlTags(text);
  text = stripUrls(text);
  text = text
    .replace(/\|/g, ':')
    .replace(/[\n\r]+/g, ' ')
    .replace(/[\[\]<>]/g, '');
  return collapseSpaces(text);
}

function sanitizePlainText(rawText, maxLength) {
  const text = toPlainText(rawText);
  if (!maxLength || text.length <= maxLength) return text;
  return truncateAtWord(text, maxLength);
}

function sanitizeExcerpt(rawText, maxLength) {
  return sanitizePlainText(rawText, maxLength);
}

function truncateAtWord(text, maxLength) {
  if (!text || text.length <= maxLength) return text;
  let cut = text.substring(0, maxLength);
  const lastSpace = cut.lastIndexOf(' ');
  if (lastSpace > Math.floor(maxLength * 0.6)) cut = cut.substring(0, lastSpace);
  cut = cut.replace(/[.,;:!?\-\s]+$/, '');
  return cut + '...';
}

function formatRelativeDate(targetDate, showTime, showDay, timeAboveDate) {
  if (!targetDate || isNaN(targetDate.getTime())) return '';
  if (!showTime && !showDay) return '';

  const now = new Date();
  const today = new Date(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), now.getDate());
  const yesterday = new Date(today);
  yesterday.setDate(yesterday.getDate() - 1);

  const itemDay = new Date(targetDate.getFullYear(), targetDate.getMonth(), targetDate.getDate());
  const clockTime = targetDate.toLocaleTimeString('en-GB', { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit' });

  let dateStr = '';
  if (itemDay.getTime() === today.getTime()) {
    dateStr = 'Today';
  } else if (itemDay.getTime() === yesterday.getTime()) {
    dateStr = 'Yesterday';
  } else {
    dateStr = targetDate.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short' });
  }

  if (showTime && showDay) {
    return timeAboveDate ? `${clockTime}<br>${dateStr}` : `${dateStr} ${clockTime}`;
  } else if (showTime) {
    return clockTime;
  } else if (showDay) {
    return dateStr;
  }
  return '';
}

return run();
:::

#### Settings you can change

| Setting | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `maxItems` | Maximum rows in the table, across every feed |
| `showTimestamp` | Show or hide the Published column |
| `showTime` | Show the clock time (for example `17:45`) |
| `showDay` | Show **Today**, **Yesterday**, or a short date |
| `showTimeAboveDate` | Put the time above the date with a line break. Set `false` for one line |
| `showExcerpt` | Show the short summary under each headline |
| `maxExcerptLength` | Character cap for each summary. Summaries are plain text (HTML and URLs removed) and stop at a whole word |
| `showImage` | Show or hide the Image column |
| `imageSize` | Markdown image size. `200` is width, `x80` is height, `120x80` is both |
| `columnOrder` | Left-to-right columns. Use `source`, `image`, `headline`, and `timestamp` |

Each item in `feeds` has:

| Field | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `url` | The RSS or Atom URL |
| `label` | Text on the source chip |
| `icon` | Phosphor name without `ph-` (for example `newspaper`, `star`, `cpu`) |
| `color` | Cell background. A theme token such as `@markerTint1` follows the dashboard theme. A hex value such as `#E11D48` stays that color |
| `maxExcerpts` | How many rows from this feed keep a summary |

Rename the table headers in `COLUMN_META` if you want another language (for example **Bron** / **Artikel** / **Geplaatst**).

With a single feed, the **Source** column hides on its own. You still see headline, image, and time.

### 4. Combine several feeds

You can also keep each site in its own **Text** widget. Copy the single-feed script, change the URL, and send each Result to a different topic. That gives you two (or more) separate news boxes.

To mix sites in one table, add more objects to the `feeds` array. The script merges them, sorts by the time each article was published (newest first), then keeps `maxItems` rows. The **Source** column comes back so you can tell the sites apart.

Put a comma after every feed except the last one. The last feed ends with `}` and then the closing `]`, with no extra comma. A comma after that last feed is a common typing mistake and HomeyScript will fail.

Use different `color` and `icon` values per feed so the chips stay readable. `maxExcerpts` lets one site show more summaries than another.

Copy this full version when you want two BBC sections in one widget:

::: code-block Two RSS feeds
// HomeyScript: RSS feed to Dashboard Studio Markdown
// Paste this into a HomeyScript, then send the Result tag to Dashboard Studio.

const CONFIG = {
  maxItems: 15,

  showTimestamp: true,
  showTime: true,
  showDay: true,
  showTimeAboveDate: true,

  showExcerpt: true,
  maxExcerptLength: 240,

  showImage: true,
  imageSize: '200',

  // Column keys: 'source', 'image', 'headline', 'timestamp'
  // The source column hides automatically when you have only one feed.
  columnOrder: ['source', 'image', 'headline', 'timestamp'],

  feeds: [
    {
      url: 'https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/entertainment_and_arts/rss.xml',
      label: 'Entertainment',
      icon: 'star',
      color: '#E11D48',
      maxExcerpts: 7
    },
    {
      url: 'https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml',
      label: 'Technology',
      icon: 'cpu',
      color: '@markerTint2',
      maxExcerpts: 7
    }
  ]
};

const COLUMN_META = {
  source: { title: 'Source', align: ':---' },
  image: { title: 'Image', align: ':---:' },
  headline: { title: 'Headline', align: ':---' },
  timestamp: { title: 'Published', align: ':---:' }
};

async function run() {
  let allItems = [];
  const excerptCounters = {};

  for (const feed of CONFIG.feeds) {
    excerptCounters[feed.url] = 0;
    const items = await fetchAndParseFeed(feed);
    allItems = allItems.concat(items);
  }

  allItems.sort((a, b) => b.date - a.date);
  allItems = allItems.slice(0, CONFIG.maxItems);

  const activeColumns = CONFIG.columnOrder.filter(col => {
    if (col === 'timestamp' && !CONFIG.showTimestamp) return false;
    if (col === 'source' && CONFIG.feeds.length <= 1) return false;
    if (col === 'image' && !CONFIG.showImage) return false;
    return true;
  });

  let markdown = '';
  markdown += '| ' + activeColumns.map(col => COLUMN_META[col].title).join(' | ') + ' |\n';
  markdown += '| ' + activeColumns.map(col => COLUMN_META[col].align).join(' | ') + ' |\n';

  for (const item of allItems) {
    const rowCells = activeColumns.map(col => {
      switch (col) {
        case 'source': {
          const bgPrefix = item.feed.color ? `[cell ${item.feed.color}] ` : '';
          const cleanIcon = item.feed.icon ? item.feed.icon.replace(/^ph-/, '') : '';
          const iconString = cleanIcon ? `:ph-${cleanIcon}|20: ` : '';
          const labelString = item.feed.label || '';
          return `${bgPrefix}${iconString}${labelString}`.trim();
        }
        case 'image':
          if (item.image) {
            const sizeModifier = CONFIG.imageSize ? `|${CONFIG.imageSize}` : '';
            return `![${sizeModifier}](${item.image})`;
          }
          return '';
        case 'headline': {
          let cellContent = `### [${item.title}](${item.link} ^)`;
          const maxAllowedExcerpts = item.feed.maxExcerpts !== undefined ? item.feed.maxExcerpts : CONFIG.maxItems;
          if (CONFIG.showExcerpt && item.excerpt) {
            if (excerptCounters[item.feed.url] < maxAllowedExcerpts) {
              cellContent += `<br>[color @textMuted]${item.excerpt}[/color]`;
              excerptCounters[item.feed.url]++;
            }
          }
          return cellContent;
        }
        case 'timestamp':
          return formatRelativeDate(item.date, CONFIG.showTime, CONFIG.showDay, CONFIG.showTimeAboveDate);
        default:
          return '';
      }
    });
    markdown += '| ' + rowCells.join(' | ') + ' |\n';
  }

  if (typeof global.setTagValue === 'function') {
    await global.setTagValue('dashboard_rss_feed', { type: 'string', title: 'Dashboard RSS Feed' }, markdown);
  }

  console.log(markdown);
  return markdown;
}

async function fetchAndParseFeed(feed) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(feed.url);
    if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP Status ${response.status}`);
    const xml = await response.text();

    const isAtom = xml.includes('<entry>');
    const nodeRegex = isAtom ? /<entry>([\s\S]*?)<\/entry>/g : /<item>([\s\S]*?)<\/item>/g;
    const nodes = xml.match(nodeRegex);
    if (!nodes) return [];

    return nodes.map(node => {
      const title = extractTagValue(node, 'title');
      const link = isAtom ? extractAtomLink(node) : extractTagValue(node, 'link');
      const dateStr = isAtom
        ? (extractTagValue(node, 'updated') || extractTagValue(node, 'published'))
        : (extractTagValue(node, 'pubDate') || extractTagValue(node, 'dc:date'));
      const rawExcerpt = extractTagValue(node, isAtom ? 'summary' : 'description');

      return {
        title: sanitizePlainText(title, 0),
        link: String(link || '').trim(),
        excerpt: sanitizeExcerpt(rawExcerpt, CONFIG.maxExcerptLength),
        image: extractImageUrl(node),
        date: dateStr ? new Date(dateStr) : new Date(0),
        feed: feed
      };
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`[Feed Error] Failed fetching ${feed.url}:`, error.message);
    return [];
  }
}

function extractTagValue(xmlBlock, tagName) {
  const match = xmlBlock.match(new RegExp(`<${tagName}(?:\\s+[^>]*)?>([\\s\\S]*?)<\/${tagName}>`, 'i'));
  if (!match) return '';
  return match[1].replace(/<!\[CDATA\[([\s\S]*?)\]\]>/gi, '$1').trim();
}

function extractAtomLink(xmlBlock) {
  const hrefMatch = xmlBlock.match(/<link\s+[^>]*href=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  return hrefMatch ? hrefMatch[1] : extractTagValue(xmlBlock, 'link');
}

function extractImageUrl(xmlBlock) {
  let match = xmlBlock.match(/<enclosure\s+[^>]*url=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  if (match) return match[1];
  match = xmlBlock.match(/<media:(?:content|thumbnail)\s+[^>]*url=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  if (match) return match[1];
  match = xmlBlock.match(/<img\s+[^>]*src=["']([^"']+)["']/i);
  if (match) return match[1];
  return null;
}

function decodeHtmlEntities(text) {
  return String(text || '')
    .replace(/&nbsp;/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/&#(\d+);/g, function (_, n) { return String.fromCharCode(parseInt(n, 10)); })
    .replace(/&#x([0-9a-f]+);/gi, function (_, n) { return String.fromCharCode(parseInt(n, 16)); })
    .replace(/&quot;/g, '"')
    .replace(/&apos;|&#39;/g, "'")
    .replace(/&lt;/g, '<')
    .replace(/&gt;/g, '>')
    .replace(/&amp;/g, '&');
}

function stripHtmlTags(text) {
  return String(text || '')
    .replace(/<script[\s\S]*?<\/script>/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/<style[\s\S]*?<\/style>/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ');
}

function stripUrls(text) {
  return String(text || '')
    .replace(/https?:\/\/[^\s<>"']+/gi, ' ')
    .replace(/www\.[^\s<>"']+/gi, ' ');
}

function collapseSpaces(text) {
  return String(text || '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
}

function toPlainText(rawText) {
  let text = decodeHtmlEntities(rawText);
  text = decodeHtmlEntities(text);
  text = stripHtmlTags(text);
  text = stripUrls(text);
  text = text
    .replace(/\|/g, ':')
    .replace(/[\n\r]+/g, ' ')
    .replace(/[\[\]<>]/g, '');
  return collapseSpaces(text);
}

function sanitizePlainText(rawText, maxLength) {
  const text = toPlainText(rawText);
  if (!maxLength || text.length <= maxLength) return text;
  return truncateAtWord(text, maxLength);
}

function sanitizeExcerpt(rawText, maxLength) {
  return sanitizePlainText(rawText, maxLength);
}

function truncateAtWord(text, maxLength) {
  if (!text || text.length <= maxLength) return text;
  let cut = text.substring(0, maxLength);
  const lastSpace = cut.lastIndexOf(' ');
  if (lastSpace > Math.floor(maxLength * 0.6)) cut = cut.substring(0, lastSpace);
  cut = cut.replace(/[.,;:!?\-\s]+$/, '');
  return cut + '...';
}

function formatRelativeDate(targetDate, showTime, showDay, timeAboveDate) {
  if (!targetDate || isNaN(targetDate.getTime())) return '';
  if (!showTime && !showDay) return '';

  const now = new Date();
  const today = new Date(now.getFullYear(), now.getMonth(), now.getDate());
  const yesterday = new Date(today);
  yesterday.setDate(yesterday.getDate() - 1);

  const itemDay = new Date(targetDate.getFullYear(), targetDate.getMonth(), targetDate.getDate());
  const clockTime = targetDate.toLocaleTimeString('en-GB', { hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit' });

  let dateStr = '';
  if (itemDay.getTime() === today.getTime()) {
    dateStr = 'Today';
  } else if (itemDay.getTime() === yesterday.getTime()) {
    dateStr = 'Yesterday';
  } else {
    dateStr = targetDate.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short' });
  }

  if (showTime && showDay) {
    return timeAboveDate ? `${clockTime}<br>${dateStr}` : `${dateStr} ${clockTime}`;
  } else if (showTime) {
    return clockTime;
  } else if (showDay) {
    return dateStr;
  }
  return '';
}

return run();
:::

